<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karaikal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karaikal is a coastal town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coromandel-coast">Coromandel Coast</a> of south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the Kaveri delta. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> acquired it from the Raja of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> in 1739 and governed it as part of French India until its de facto transfer to India in 1954, completed legally in 1962. It forms a district of the Union Territory of Puducherry, although it is surrounded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karaikal.jpg" alt="Karaikal" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: P Jeganathan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karaikal_Beach_JEG2443.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
